8vqn|v|To cause to become sour; to cause to turn from sweet to sour; as, exposure to the air sours many substances. ; To make cold and unproductive, as soil. ; To make unhappy, uneasy, or less agreeable. ; To cause or permit to become harsh or unkindly. ; To macerate, and render fit for plaster or mortar; as, to sour lime for business purposes. ; To become sour; to turn from sweet to sour; as, milk soon sours in hot weather; a kind temper sometimes sours in adversity.	o:3u1m,79,10;1xx1,71,26;74hd,63,1;1gix,62,1;23xw,46,1;5lab,43,1;5tf1,38,5;7vln,38,11;1giy,37,1;u88,36,4;56sm,34,1;9b6a,30,2;7vm0,30,5;3e6o,29,1;9f7x,24,2~1xx1,71,26;7vln,38,11;3u1m,79,10;7vm0,30,5;5tf1,38,5;3e5j,19,5;u88,36,4;xb3,18,2;9f7x,24,2;5vno,9,2;9b6a,30,2;3hsp,21,2;148b,22,2;88ow,2,1;5lab,43,1	s:9f86,72,11;aj7s,66,2;8sca,54,5;ykl,48,2;tva,47,5;9f7x,39,6;9b6a,20,1;93jo,20,2;36hp,8,1~9f86,72,11;9f7x,39,6;8sca,54,5;tva,47,5;aj7s,66,2;ykl,48,2;93jo,20,2;36hp,8,1;9b6a,20,1	d:71cn,31,3;9f7x,24,2;7nk2,21,9;5hzr,19,4;8rmr,10,6~7nk2,21,9;8rmr,10,6;5hzr,19,4;71cn,31,3;9f7x,24,2
